Miners now re-propose a block after `miner.transient_rejection_retry_timeout_ms` (default 5 seconds) when some signers rejected it for a transient reason (`NoSignerConsensus`, `ConsensusHashMismatch`, `NoSortitionView`, `ConnectivityIssues`, or an `UnknownParent`/`NotFoundError` validation failure), instead of waiting for the full rejection-based timeout (e.g. 90 seconds). This removes a long stall at the start of a tenure when a few signers are slow to converge after a new burn block.
